# ===========================================================================
#  This repository stores CONTENT-HASHED files.
#
#  packwiz records the sha256 of the bytes as they exist on disk, and both the
#  .mrpack manifest and the installer verify against those hashes. If git
#  rewrites line endings on checkout or commit, the bytes change and every
#  hash check fails ("Hash invalid!").
#
#  So: never touch line endings, anywhere. `-text` tells git to treat every
#  file as raw bytes instead of text it may normalise.
# ===========================================================================
* -text

# Keep the pack itself explicitly byte-exact even if someone edits this file.
pack/** -text
